##### Decision Variables

$x_{ij}\geq0$: quantity shipped from store $i\in I$ to customer group $j\in J$ (continuous).

##### Objective Function

$\min\sum_{i\in I}\sum_{j\in J}c_{ij}x_{ij}$

##### Constraints

1. Demand: $\sum_{i\in I}x_{ij}\geq d_j,\quad\forall j\in J$.
2. Supply capacity: $\sum_{j\in J}x_{ij}\leq s_i,\quad\forall i\in I$.
3. Non-negativity: $x_{ij}\geq0$ continuous.

$I=\{S1,S2,S3\}$ and $J=\{C1,C2,C3,C4\}$. CSV matrix rows are stores and columns are customer groups. Total supply is 2083 and total demand is 2046; unused supply is allowed. All transportation costs are positive, so excess deliveries cannot improve the minimum cost.


